            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "AI findings (partial):\r\n\r\n> The PR doesn't close the hole it targets\r\n> \r\n> 1. **Huge positive `ue_size` still crashes** (`undo.c:1093`). Only `< 0` is rejected. Use `0x7FFFFFF0` instead of `0xFFFFFFFF` in this PR's own repro and you get `xmalloc(8 * 2147483632)` ≈ 17 GB plus a 17 GB `memset`: \r\n> `preserve_exit(e_outofmem)` on a 200-byte file, or an OOM-kill with overcommit.\r\n> \r\n> 2. **The three sibling fields are read unvalidated** (`undo.c:1088-1090`): `ue_top`, `ue_bot`, `ue_lcount`. This is worse than what's being fixed. `u_undoredo` (`undo.c:2318`) guards only\r\n> \r\n>     ```c\r\n>     if (top > curbuf->b_ml.ml_line_count || top >= bot || bot > curbuf->b_ml.ml_line_count + 1)\r\n>     ```\r\n> \r\n>     With `top = -5`, `bot = -1` all three are false, so it proceeds into `ml_delete()` with negative lnums, giving a negative `db_index[]` subscript in `ml_delete_int()`. Heap OOB read, not just an OOM abort. Same corrupted-file threat \r\n> model, still open.\r\n\r\n",
